  "_doc": "Formable nations (docs/NATIONS.md). region: rules over the shared admin-1 map (iso = ISO-3 codes, optional box [lonMin, latMin, lonMax, latMax] on the province centre, optional names); a country may form the nation when it owns at least `need` of the region's provinces, its capital lies in one of `capitalIn` (ISO-3) or its tag is in `tags`, its technology era is within `eras` [first, last], it is not a subject and its stability is at least the minimum in nations.json. `is`: tags that already are this nation (they cannot form it, and while one exists nobody can); TAG@scenario limits a tag to one scenario. Forming renames the country, sets its flag (`flag` = file under data/flags/ without .svg; `flagEras` picks an older flag before an era; null or no file = the drawn `pattern`), may change its colour, grants the `trait`, prestige, stability and legitimacy, and claims on every province of the region it does not own.",
